# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b2), edited. finneas_trout's first conversation.

~ start
set finneas_trout_met
Narrator: Ink, damp paper, and tallow smoke cling to the young man's cuffs. He adjusts his spectacles, bright and restless as a city lecturer.
finneas_trout [smile]: Good evening! Wide-awake strangers from beyond the mist, I gather. I am Finneas Trout of Baskerton, teaching this village basic reason.
* Ask for a lesson on the realm's lore -> shop_open
* Ask how a Baskerton scholar fares in Wickermoor -> about_self
* Ask about his studies of the Grey -> about_village
* Ask after the strange double he saw -> rumour
* [Insight DC 12] Notice the fine scented candles stacked on his desk -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ menu
finneas_trout [neutral]: Do ask if a question occurs to you. Inquiry is our best lantern against local superstition.
* Ask for a lesson on the realm's lore -> shop_open
* Ask how a Baskerton scholar fares in Wickermoor -> about_self
* Ask about his studies of the Grey -> about_village
* Ask after the strange double he saw -> rumour
* [Insight DC 12] Notice the fine scented candles stacked on his desk -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
finneas_trout [smile]: Gladly! Let us begin with the geography of Druskenvald and the six bells of the night.
-> menu

~ about_self
finneas_trout [weary]: I lodge at the inn and teach children that thunder is weather, not an angry spirit. Mayor Somerton means well, though his love of old customs tries my patience.
-> menu

~ about_village
finneas_trout [neutral]: I am charting the Grey, a malady where folk lose colour and heart until they fade into stupor. Superstition blames curses, yet every affliction has a mechanism.
-> menu

~ rumour
finneas_trout [afraid]: I could swear I saw the spitting image of one of your party pass the inn before the recent murders began.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: Half a dozen beeswax tapers sit wrapped in twine beside his inkwell, far more than one small room needs.
finneas_trout [smile]: Those are from Oswick Frey's chandlery, as I read late. Mr. Frey is a remarkably thoughtful conversationalist for such a rustic parish.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
finneas_trout [neutral]: A scholar goes through a dreadful number of candles in a realm without a sunrise.
-> menu
